==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
<!--from Wikipedia's article:-->
Uncertain: possibly from Cruft Hall, the name of the radar laboratory of [[w:Harvard|Harvard]]'s physics department during the Second World War, which contained much old and unused technical equipment; possibly a [[blend]] of '''[[crust]]''' and '''[[fluff]]''', both of which suggest things that are obsolete and superfluous; possibly a modified form of '''crust'''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ʌft|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|computing|informal|lang=en}} Anything old or of inferior quality.
# {{context|computing|informal|lang=en}} Redundant, old or improperly written [[code]], especially that which accumulates over time; [[clutter]].

